  "chapter": 656,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 56 Chapter 656\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 6532-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\n        permitting kelp cultivation in underwater  lands  at  Gardiner's\n        and Peconic bays and commercial fishing licenses\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill would amend the Environmental Conservation Law to authorize\nkelp  cultivation  in  underwater  lands  ceded  to  Suffolk  County  in\nGardiner's and Peconic Bay. The cultivation of kelp will provide signif-\nicant  environmental  and  economic benefits to the State. Kelp not only\nremoves carbon dioxide and nitrogen from the environment but its useful-\nness as an ingredient in food, cosmetics  and  other  consumer  products\nmakes  kelp a valuable crop in aquaculture. The Executive fully supports\nthe goals of this bill but requires technical edits to ensure the  bene-\nfits of this legislation can be fully realized and to make the bill more\neasily implemented by the Department of Environmental Conservation.\n \n  To this end the Executive secured an agreement with the Legislature to\nmake these technical amendments in a bill to be introduced next session.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
